  "summary": "Bursting with aromatic warmth, this <b>vegetarian Moroccan stew</b> highlights vibrant plant-based ingredients slow-simmered in a conical clay tagine. Nutritious <b>cooked chickpeas</b> and sweet butternut squash anchor the dish, absorbing the complex flavors of ras el hanout, ground cinnamon, and warm ginger. Dried apricots dissolve subtly into the rich tomato broth, creating a delicate sweet-and-savory contrast that defines traditional North African cookery. Soft zucchini slices and caramelised red onions complete the vibrant vegetable medley, making this dish both hearty and visually stunning. Simmered gently over low heat, the ingredients meld together into a deeply satisfying stew that requires no meat to deliver robust depth. Sprinkled with crunchy <b>toasted flaked almonds</b> and fresh herbs just before serving, this colorful tagine offers balanced textures and incredible spice aromas. Pair it with a mound of fluffy steamed couscous or warm flatbread to soak up every last drop of the fragrant, spiced sauce.",
